# Rule file authoring

Applies when creating or editing `.cursor/rules/*.mdc`. For templates, see **write-cursor-rules** skill (`.cursor/skills/write-cursor-rules/`).

## Required frontmatter

```yaml
---
description: One line for the rule picker
globs: **/*.ts          # when file-scoped
alwaysApply: false      # true = every chat
---
```

| Field | Notes |
|-------|-------|
| `description` | Required, specific |
| `alwaysApply` | `true` = omit `globs` |
| `globs` | Required when `alwaysApply: false` |

Filename: kebab-case, e.g. `typescript-logging.mdc`.

## Body style

- **One concern per file** — split if over ~50 lines or multiple stacks
- **Actionable** bullets — not vague "write clean code"
- **❌ BAD / ✅ GOOD** snippets when patterns matter
- Project-specific facts only
- Under **500 lines** hard cap

## Workflow

1. Clarify purpose, scope (`alwaysApply` vs `globs`)
2. Draft frontmatter + title + sections
3. Run validation checklist
4. Write `.cursor/rules/<name>.mdc`

## Validation checklist

- [ ] Valid YAML frontmatter
- [ ] `description` matches body
- [ ] Single concern
- [ ] No secrets in examples

## Do not

- Duplicate User Rules from Cursor settings into project rules
- Put slash-command authoring here — use **command-author** for `.cursor/commands/`
